00:52:57.510 --> 00:52:58.470
Wonder where he gets that.

1219
00:53:00.990 --> 00:53:06.070
Well, we were discussing getting new water bottles for school, you know, the reusable

1220
00:53:06.070 --> 00:53:08.130
ones, and this got us on bottled water.

1221
00:53:08.270 --> 00:53:14.310
And my son ended up doing a whole deep dive for our family on the origins of bottled water.

1222
00:53:14.510 --> 00:53:19.550
And I thought I would share a little bit about it since what the coincidence that David Wallace

1223
00:53:19.550 --> 00:53:20.970
is holding a water bottle.

1224
00:53:20.970 --> 00:53:21.470
Okay.

1225
00:53:22.150 --> 00:53:27.530
This is my son's deep dive, and I find it fascinating, and I think you will too, even though you're

1226
00:53:27.530 --> 00:53:28.110
not his mother.

1227
00:53:28.430 --> 00:53:36.330
The first commercially distributed bottled water company in America was called Jackson Spa,

1228
00:53:36.410 --> 00:53:40.890
and it was founded in 1767 in Boston.

1229
00:53:41.450 --> 00:53:45.850
This was the question that launched everything was, who made the first bottled water?

1230
00:53:45.970 --> 00:53:46.070
Right, right.

1231
00:53:46.070 --> 00:53:50.390
It was Jackson Spa, and the people who drank the water thought that it held therapeutic

1232
00:53:50.390 --> 00:53:54.590
properties because it came from, like, one of those mineral springs, a natural spring.

1233
00:53:54.970 --> 00:53:59.870
One of the biggies, Arrowhead, was established in 1917.

1234
00:54:00.170 --> 00:54:01.350
That's so early.

1235
00:54:01.570 --> 00:54:02.230
I know.

1236
00:54:02.990 --> 00:54:07.510
Arrowhead water is sourced from the mountain springs in California, Colorado, and Canada.

1237
00:54:07.710 --> 00:54:09.890
It's bottled in California, even today.

1238
00:54:10.370 --> 00:54:11.890
Then we get up to Evian.

1239
00:54:11.890 --> 00:54:18.310
That was not established until 1978, almost 70 years after Arrowhead.

1240
00:54:18.510 --> 00:54:21.530
Their water comes from a spring in the French Alps.

1241
00:54:21.870 --> 00:54:25.670
Fiji water, as held by David Wallace, comes from Fiji.

1242
00:54:26.110 --> 00:54:31.770
But the big shift in bottled water came when Pepsi and Coca-Cola got into the game by selling

1243
00:54:31.770 --> 00:54:33.290
purified water.

1244
00:54:34.370 --> 00:54:41.250
Purified water is basically municipal tap water, which is then filtered using a process called

1245
00:54:41.250 --> 00:54:42.630
reverse osmosis.

1246
00:54:42.890 --> 00:54:48.570
Spring water is also filtered, but the reverse osmosis is what purifies it, I guess.

1247
00:54:48.730 --> 00:54:49.910
That's the purified part.

1248
00:54:50.190 --> 00:54:53.430
Then we all wondered as a family, what's the best water?

1249
00:54:53.850 --> 00:54:56.170
Purified, spring, tap?

1250
00:54:56.810 --> 00:54:58.010
You know what it is?

1251
00:54:58.850 --> 00:54:59.490
Guess.

1252
00:54:59.850 --> 00:55:00.330
Tap.

1253
00:55:00.750 --> 00:55:01.190
Nope.

1254
00:55:01.730 --> 00:55:01.990
Spring.

1255
00:55:02.270 --> 00:55:02.550
Nope.

1256
00:55:03.230 --> 00:55:03.790
Purified.

1257
00:55:03.970 --> 00:55:04.530
Yes.

1258
00:55:05.890 --> 00:55:06.870
Purified water.

1259
00:55:07.390 --> 00:55:12.370
The reverse osmosis makes it the most pure above filtered spring or tap.

1260
00:55:12.890 --> 00:55:13.930
How about that?

1261
00:55:14.250 --> 00:55:20.790
Pepsi and Coke were already using purified water as the basis of their sodas.

1262
00:55:20.930 --> 00:55:24.250
So they would get water, they would purify it, and then they would add all the bubbles,

1263
00:55:24.330 --> 00:55:27.390
and then they would add all the other stuff that you put in a soda.

1264
00:55:27.670 --> 00:55:27.930
Yeah.

1265
00:55:28.390 --> 00:55:33.810
And so it was really easy for them to just start bottling it, you know, before they did

1266
00:55:33.810 --> 00:55:35.330
all the rest of it to make it a soda.

1267
00:55:35.950 --> 00:55:38.230
Well, I think that's a fascinating deep dive.

1268
00:55:38.410 --> 00:55:39.010
Well done.

